      "content": "It is completely understandable that when you feel this profoundly empty, the idea of \"getting better\" feels like a cruel joke. That constant, heavy nothingness is a real state of being, and it's exhausting to fight. While the grayness might feel permanent right now, reaching out to a therapist can help you find tools to navigate it, even if it doesn't instantly erase it. Please consider speaking with a professional who can help you manage this feeling of being disconnected.",
      "source": "target",
